course: dictionary
lesson: 5686
title: Words from Scotland: loch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A loch is a lake, and you will meet the word in Scotland and in stories set there. Look at the clues around it. «In Edinburgh, Otto's dad takes him fishing by the loch (Scots for lake).» The words in brackets tell you what loch means, so you do not need a dictionary.
explain: Some lochs reach the sea. A sea loch is a long, narrow arm of the sea that stretches into the land. Read the sentence «Loch Ness in Scotland, long, narrow and over 200 metres deep» and you can picture a long, narrow lake.
explain: Ireland has a similar word, «lough», which also means lake. Say loch with the ch sound at the back of your throat, as in the Scottish word.
fact: A loch is a lake in Scotland.
fact: A sea loch is a long, narrow arm of the sea that reaches into the land.
fact: Loch Ness is over 200 metres deep, and the Loch Ness Monster legend comes from it.
fact: In Ireland, the similar word is «lough».
fact: The famous 1934 Loch Ness monster photo was a fake made with a toy.
exercise: «In Edinburgh, Otto's dad takes him fishing by the loch (Scots for lake).» What is a loch? | *A lake | A type of bird | Mountain | A sandy beach
exercise: Which word is the Irish word for a loch? | moor | bay | glen | *lough
exercise: What is a sea loch? | *A long, narrow arm of the sea that reaches into the land | A tall hill covered in heather | A dry valley with no water | A small river that flows into a lake
test:
What famous legend comes from Loch Ness? | The Beast of Dartmoor | The Kraken of Norway | *The Loch Ness Monster | The Giant of the Lake District
test:
Which sentence uses loch correctly? | «We sailed across the desert on camels.» | «The loch was full of sand and dry grass.» | *«We walked along the shore of the loch and watched the water.» | «The loch rang with church bells.»
exam:
Which fact about Loch Ness comes from the lesson? | It is in Wales | Its name means sea in Irish | *It is over 200 metres deep | It is the smallest lake in the UK
